PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key facts: cholesterol required specifically for ecdysone (molting); cholestanol supplies only bulk/membrane sterol; 250 mg/L chol supports full dev., 2 mg/L does not; adult survival = 0 on pure 250 mg/L cholestanol. Maternal provisioning deposits usable sterol into eggs when mothers on cholesterol.

Major split: B (both no eclosion) vs. C (Death, no eclosion) vs. D (both normal). C arguments strongest: maternal reserve suffices for larval molts but is exhausted before metamorphosis on pure cholestanol (hence larval death or failure to eclose, matching adult-survival datum); scenario 2 lacks any reserve and 2 mg/L remains sub-threshold, blocking eclosion. D ignores adult-survival datum and insufficiency of 2 mg/L. B underestimates maternal carry-over for early stages.

Unresolved: exact timing of lethality (larval death vs. pupal arrest) when reserve is finite. No support for regressive development or impossible-to-determine. Current lean: C (60 %).}

